Changelog: 26-10-2026 22:54:30

Added. portable: Pane, the detail pane (a card's surface for what the focused card shows). The window registers
the bundled Inter itself, and the legend's old buttons leave at once when it changes; they were only detached
first, which on the Ally could take the focus events from the window (found while building Windows Portable Test).
The header's status line (battery and time) is 18 pt bold in the text color, level with the header's top, its parts
divided by a bar (owner, 26-10-2026: 13 pt dimmed was too small).

Changelog: 26-10-2026 22:37:18

Added. portable: the portable window of the Windows Portable Suite (owner, 26-10-2026: direction D, B's amber on C's
cards). PORTABLE is its design as a theme for core's widgets; PortableHeader, Card, Pill, Legend and PortableWindow
are what its apps are built of. Sizes are the mock-up's at 1280 x 720 and scale with the screen. The focused card
is raised with an amber edge and glow; a focused pill is dimmed. The d-pad, the left stick or the arrow keys move the
focus to the nearest card or pill, A or Enter acts, B or Escape goes back, and a page binds its own buttons (X, Y,
LB, RB). The controller counts only while the window is active.

Added. gamepad: a game controller read with pygame-ce for the portable window: the window's actions (a held
direction repeats) and every button, stick and trigger as it is, for a controller test. Without pygame-ce or a
controller nothing happens. The BC250 portal keeps its own gamepad.py.

Changelog: 26-10-2026 22:01:21

Added. applog: an app can name its suite (log_file() and setup() take suite=), and its log goes to the suite's
folder: %LOCALAPPDATA%\windows-portable-suite\<app id>\<app id>.log for the Windows Portable Suite's apps. An app
that names none keeps ~/.local/share/<app id>/<app id>.log, as before.

Changelog: 26-10-2026 21:46:30

Added. platform: the Windows side, for the Windows Portable Suite. suite_data() and suite_config() give a suite's
folder (%LOCALAPPDATA% and %APPDATA% on Windows, the XDG folders elsewhere), start_menu() the Start-menu programs
folder, open_path() opens a file, folder or URL with its own program (os.startfile on Windows, xdg-open elsewhere),
launch_in_terminal() runs a PowerShell command in a window of its own on Windows (powershell_command(): the exit file
and the "Press Enter" pause as with bash), and make_shortcut() writes a Windows shortcut. PATH_BUDGET (240 of
Windows' 260 characters) is what a suite's paths stay within. data_home(), config_home(), bin_home() and xdg_open()
are unchanged on every system, and nothing changes on Linux.

Changelog: 26-10-2026 20:45:22

Fixed. The tests run on Windows: wifi's skip there (sysfs and kernel modules), as do the instance tests that run the
server and the client in one thread (a named pipe on Windows; two processes reach each other, as two launches of an
app do), and the SteamGridDB key's file mode is checked on Linux only. The code is unchanged.

Changelog: 26-10-2026 13:21:15

Added. widgets: the theme the widgets draw with can be set (set_theme(), current_theme(), accent()), and
create_app(theme=) sets the one an app passes: an app that is not a suite's draws with its own design (owner,
26-10-2026: Nexus Releases takes Nexus's). Without one the suite's chosen theme applies, as before; theme.py is
unchanged, so the apps' copies of it stay equal.

