Changelog: 15-10-2026 03:27:56

Version 0.1.4.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 02:31:31

No translations: create_app() and run_app() take no lang any more and load no translator (Qt's own, core's or the app's); AppInfo loses translations_dir, catalog and languages, and DEFAULT_LANGUAGES is gone; help keeps HelpView and loses HelpPage, which only added a language picker; updates and widgets use their English text directly. text.fmt() and fill() stay, for placeholders. Tests follow.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 02:10:51

Version 0.1.3.

Changelog: 15-10-2026 02:01:27

instance: a second launch can hand its arguments to the running instance. already_running(app_id, args) sends them after the show request as an args line (a JSON list), and serve(app_id, window, on_args) gives them to on_args in the running instance, after showing the window. Without arguments the request is the plain show request it always was; an instance without on_args, or one on an older core, only shows its window; a malformed args line is dropped. For the apps that open what they are given on the command line (Bazzite pkgxtractor, Bazzite NetcatGUI, Bazzite UMD File Renamer). RoundedToolTip.install removes its event filter when the app quits (aboutToQuit): the filter saw the events of widgets and sockets destroyed after the event loop had ended, while Python was tearing down, which crashed Bazzite NetcatGUI at exit. Tests: test_instance (the plain request unchanged, the arguments handed over, no handler or a bad line only shows), test_widgets (the filter removed on quit).

Changelog: 14-10-2026 00:36:43

New module steam: Steam's own files for apps that add non-Steam games for Game Mode. Finding Steam and its users, whether it runs (a zombie steam process does not count), closing it for a change and starting it again (with_steam_closed), the binary shortcuts.vdf (read_vdf, write_vdf), a non-Steam game's appid, the shortcut's fields in Steam's order (shortcut_entry), adding, updating (the play time kept) and removing shortcuts beside the others, and write_shortcuts(), which writes several shortcuts and their artwork for every Steam user, each file once. Moved from BC250 Console Link (its own code, there AGPL-3.0-or-later, relicensed by the owner to GPL-3.0-or-later for core, 14-10-2026), which now uses it; tests/test_steam.py covers it.

Changelog: 12-10-2026 08:07:21

AppHeader in widgets: the first line of every app window, the icon at 96 px spanning the title row (name with the version, states, actions) and a second row (status boxes or main controls), as Bazzite Test and the Governor Manager draw it. test_widgets checks the layout.

Changelog: 11-10-2026 20:58:28

MetricBox centers its value and caption by default, like Bazzite Test's stats boxes; centered=False keeps them left-aligned. test_widgets checks the default; test_parity compares centered and left-aligned boxes with both governor's and helixsr's copies.

Changelog: 11-10-2026 19:02:46

instance.py: Two launches at the same moment (a double-click on a Desktop icon that opens on one click) no longer
open two windows. Both found no running instance, since the window and its socket take a while to appear, and the
second then removed the first one's socket. The first launch now takes a lock file at once; a launch that finds it
taken waits up to 10 s for that instance's socket and hands over instead. A crashed instance's lock is stale, so the
next launch starts as before. The apps that bundle core (portal, Bazzite Test, ACE Queues, BIOS Reader, Memory
Manager, System Overlay, Portal dependency checker) get it with their next release. Tests in tests/test_instance.py.

Changelog: 11-10-2026 07:28:24

Version 0.1.2. Shared UI improvements

Changelog: 11-10-2026 01:05:44

Header status widget StatusText: a colored dot and the state in bold, in the color of its kind (red bad, orange warn, green ok, blue info, the normal text color for neutral), with the same set_status() and text() as StatusPill. For a state next to an app's title, where a pill is too heavy; StatusPill stays for cards.

Changelog: 10-10-2026 20:56:48

Version 0.1.1. Initial release

Changelog: 09-10-2026 22:59:08

SUITE_MANUAL_URL: the address of the suite manual on GitHub Pages. README: short, with a link to the manual.

Changelog: 09-10-2026 18:22:39

MetricBox has an optional centered=True that centers the value and caption (helixsr's header uses it); the default
renders as before. The parity test covers the centered box against helixsr's copy.

tests/test_instance.py deletes its server and window explicitly: left to Python's collection at exit, they made the
interpreter crash after the last test in about half of the runs (the tests themselves passed).

Changelog: 09-10-2026 17:51:51

New module bc250_core.instance: one running instance per app and user over a local socket (after the
governor's instance.py). A second launch hands its Wayland activation token to the running instance,
which brings its window to the front. Tests in core/tests/test_instance.py.

Changelog: 08-10-2026 22:26:29

Initial version 0.1.0 of bc250_core, the code the suite's apps share. It is bundled into each app release.
- appinfo: AppInfo.
- theme: the palette and Inter font.
- text: fmt, fill, plain_tooltip, window_title.
- widgets: StatusPill, MetricBox, ClickableLogo, Terminal, TextDialog, RoundedToolTip with show/hide_tooltip,
  page_header, hint_label, accent_button, set_button_active.
- app: create_app, run_app, exec_app.
- settings: open_settings at each app's existing file, geometry helpers, SettingsStore.
- help: HelpView, HelpPage.
- updates: latest_release with a tag prefix for the suite's per-app tags, UpdateStatus, UpdateChecker.
- platform: XDG folders, xdg_open, launch_in_terminal with an exit file.
